#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:224
msgid "How do I start investing?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:226
msgid "You can buy Tuleva Savings Fund units on Tuleva's website. It works like this:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:228
msgid "Open a Savings Fund account."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:229
msgid "Choose a suitable contribution amount and whether you want to make a one-time payment or a recurring payment. Start with as little as 1 euro."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:230
msgid "You are then directed to your bank with a payment link."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:231
msgid "Pay for the units from your current account. We recommend using an account registered as an investment account."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:232
msgid "You now own Tuleva Savings Fund units. You can see and sell your units by logging in to your Tuleva account."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:234
msgid "Fund units cannot be bought or sold through other service providers, because that would create additional costs."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:236
#, php-format
msgid "See also: %1$s and %2$s."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:237
msgid "how to open an account for a company"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:238
msgid "how to start saving for a child"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:243
msgid "Why use an investment account for contributions?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:245
msgid "When investing as a private person, we recommend using an investment account to buy Savings Fund units. This makes sense because it lets you defer your income tax liability until you sell your investments and take the money out of the investment account."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:246
msgid "So if you don't have one yet, open an investment account at a bank and transfer the money meant for the Savings Fund there. You can also have several investment accounts. Then make a transfer from the investment account to the Tuleva Savings Fund account. If at some point you want to sell Savings Fund units, the money should be paid back to the investment account."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:247
msgid "Read more: why and how to use an investment account with the Savings Fund?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:251
msgid "How do I move my assets from elsewhere?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:253
msgid "Unlike pension funds, ordinary fund units and shares cannot be automatically \"transferred\" from another service provider to Tuleva. The most cost-efficient and fastest way is the following:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:255
msgid "Sell your existing assets: sell the positions at your service provider that you want to bring to Tuleva."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:256
msgid "Wait for the money to arrive: depending on the instrument, whether a fund or a stock, it usually takes 2–3 business days for the money to arrive."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:257
msgid "Make a contribution to the Tuleva Savings Fund: once the money is in your account, log in to Tuleva and make a payment to the Savings Fund."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:259
msgid "If you invest as a private person and use an investment account, selling your assets creates no immediate income tax liability: you can reinvest the whole amount, including the gains, tax-free. If you invest from an ordinary account, you have to pay income tax on the gains from selling your existing assets with your next tax return."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:260
msgid "As an illustration, we have put together a guide for bringing assets held at Swedbank to Tuleva, that is, selling your existing assets and making a contribution to the fund. Broadly, the process is similar when selling assets at other service providers and making a contribution to the Tuleva Savings Fund."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:261
msgid "When moving assets held by a company, the sale and purchase are recorded in the company's accounts. Taxes only arise once you sell the units and take the profit out of the company."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:265
msgid "How do you get your money out?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:267
msgid "Unlike pension funds, the Tuleva Savings Fund is a UCITS fund. This means you have the right to sell your units back and withdraw your money at any time."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:268
msgid "A sale order for Savings Fund units must be submitted through Tuleva's website. The money arrives in your bank account within three business days after the redemption price is published (T+3). Where possible, we make the payment faster."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:269
msgid "In more detail, the process works like this:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:271
msgid "Order timing:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:271
msgid "if you submit a sale order on a business day before 16:00, it is considered received the same day. If you submit an order after 16:00, on a weekend, or on a public holiday, it is considered received on the next business day."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:272
msgid "Payout speed:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:272
msgid "we make the payout within three business days after the redemption price is published. For example, if you submitted a sale order on the 1st at 14:00, we publish the redemption price on the 2nd at 16:00."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:273
msgid "We make the payout only to the account you have made a contribution from. This way we can be sure the account is yours."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:278
msgid "Does the fund pay dividends?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:280
msgid "No, the fund does not make cash payouts as dividends. Instead, we automatically reinvest the earned income inside the fund."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:281
msgid "This has two main benefits. First, reinvesting dividends helps grow the fund's assets and the value of your units over time. So although no regular payouts land on your account, you still earn additional income, which is reflected in a higher unit price. Second, income tax would have to be paid on dividends, which in turn would reduce your income."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:282
msgid "If you want to get money out, you can sell fund units and make a withdrawal at any time. See the question \"How do you get your money out?\" above."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:286
msgid "How does reporting for the tax return work?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:288
msgid "If you invest as a private person and use an investment account, income tax declaration starts from the bank where you opened the investment account. You declare to the tax authority the difference between the money paid into the investment account and the money paid out of it. Contributions to Tuleva Savings Fund units must be marked as neutral in the investment account declaration if you have not sold units during the current year, in which case they are not taken into account when calculating the difference."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:289
msgid "If you invest from an ordinary current account rather than an investment account, sell fund units, and have earned income, you must declare the earned income yourself to the Estonian Tax and Customs Board when filling in your tax return. Tuleva does not withhold income tax."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:293
msgid "What return can you expect from the fund?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:295
msgid "Tuleva's goal is to earn returns over the long term. We know that the value of assets invested in the fund can swing sharply from year to year, but without taking conscious risk it is not possible to earn a high return."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:296
msgid "Our fund tracks the world's stock markets, whose historical return over the last 100 years has been roughly 7% per year. Still, this is only a long-term average: history has shown both very big growth years and periods when markets have been in a deep slump."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:297
msgid "The average return so far is no guarantee. The coming years on the stock markets may not be like the previous ones. It is possible that the fund will instead make a loss in the coming years."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:301
msgid "How are investment risks managed?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:303
msgid "First, as with any investment, the value of your investments, in other words the return, is not guaranteed. When stock markets fall, the value of a fund unit falls too. This is a natural part of investing. The main rule is still: don't invest money in stocks or stock funds that you plan to take into use in the near future."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:304
msgid "Second, there is business risk: what if something happens to Tuleva? Under the Investment Funds Act, we hold the fund's assets, meaning the fund's securities and cash, in other words your investments, strictly separate from the assets of the fund manager, Tuleva. The fund's assets are held by the depositary, AS SEB Pank. This means that even if something were to happen to Tuleva, your assets are protected, because they are strictly separated from Tuleva's own."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:305
msgid "Third, we have been asked how it is ensured that we don't use your invested money in bad faith. The terms of Tuleva's funds set out precisely where the fund manager may put investors' money. The money may only be invested in the funds in the model portfolio. These funds must meet certain conditions, for example together tracking the MSCI ACWI index and being sufficiently liquid. This is why not even a fund manager with the worst intentions could move money \"aside\" at Tuleva."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:307
#, php-format
msgid "We have also recorded %1$s about risks and diversification. You can read more in section 4.1 of the %2$s."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:308
msgid "a separate podcast episode"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:309
msgid "prospectus"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:314
msgid "For companies"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:317
msgid "Can a company invest in the Savings Fund?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:319
msgid "Yes. From June 15, 2026, an Estonian-registered private limited company with up to two shareholders, whose shareholders are at the same time board members and beneficial owners, can also invest in the fund. The same fund and the same fee as for a private person."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:323
msgid "How do I open a Savings Fund account for a company?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:325
msgid "It works like this:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:327
msgid "Log in to Tuleva's website. Fill in the questionnaire both about yourself and about the company. If the company has two shareholders, both must complete this step."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:328
msgid "You now have two profiles in Tuleva: one in your name and another in the company's name."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:329
msgid "Make the first contribution from the company's bank account. You can set up contributions and a recurring payment the same way as a private person."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:334
msgid "Do both shareholders have to take part in creating the account?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:336
msgid "Yes. If the company has two shareholders, you both have to go through verification, which means filling in a short questionnaire."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:340
msgid "What happens if the company's structure changes?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:342
msgid "If the company's structure no longer meets the conditions, for example a third shareholder joins, the company cannot acquire new fund units. In certain cases we have the right to redeem the fund units unilaterally. The value of the existing units is preserved."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:346
msgid "Do Tuleva members also earn a member bonus when investing through a company?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:348
msgid "No, when investing in the Savings Fund through a company, the company cannot earn a member bonus, because the articles of association of the Tuleva cooperative do not allow it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/savings-fund-landing-content.php:349
msgid "If you are a member of the Tuleva cooperative and invest in the Savings Fund as a private person, you earn a member bonus of 0.05% of the value of your assets every year."
msgstr ""

